#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# scan

#% text
# `scan(f, xs)` applies `f` to each element of `xs` in order, for its effects; its value is `null`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
{ var t = 0; scan(k => { t = t + k }, range(10)); t }
#% output
#= 55

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Its own value is `null`:

#% cell
scan(k => k, [1, 2]) === null
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `map`, `fold`, `map_indexed`
